   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="address">
                    <ab>
                        <address>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_CHE_ZURI_06">Seefeldstrasse 73</name> <hi rend="superscript">III</hi>
                            </addrLine>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_CHE_ZURI">Zurich</name> VIII: <name type="geo" key="G_CHE">Switzerland</name>
                            </addrLine>
                        </address> </ab>
                </div>
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <p>Dear <name type="person" key="weav76">Miss Weaver</name>: I confirm <rs type="letter" key="L_68331">my telegram</rs> <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">
                            <date when="1917-01-27">of Sunday</date>
                        </seg> in reply to your kind message. I am glad to hear that the <seg xml:id="seg2" type="note-anchor">sheets</seg> have arrived safely and hope that the <seg xml:id="seg3" type="note-anchor">
                            <rs type="work" key="W_APORTRAIT">English edition</rs>
                        </seg> will soon come out. Will you please note my new address? I must change my quarters owing to the damp of my flat.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <salute>        	With sincerest thanks and kind regards</salute>
                        <signed>                    	<name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>
                        </signed> <dateline>
                            <date when="1917-01-29">29.i.917</date>
                        </dateline>
                    </closer>
                </div>
            </div> <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">JJ is referring to his <rs type="letter" key="L_68331">telegram of Saturday, 27 January 1917</rs>.</note>
                <note xml:id="note2" target="#seg2" type="commentary">On <date when="1917-01-22">22 January 1917</date>, Harriet Weaver sent JJ a telegram telling him that the sheets from America had arrived that day (mentioned in her letter to JJ of 26 January 1917, Firth 167). For context, see <rs type="letter" key="L_68297">JJ to Weaver, 4 June 1916</rs>, note 3, “cuttings”.</note>
                <note xml:id="note3" target="#seg3" type="commentary">
                    <name type="work" key="W_APORTRAIT">A Portrait of the Artist as a Young Man</name>, eventually published in London by The Egoist Ltd. on <date when="1917-02-12">12 February 1917</date>.</note>
            </div>
      </body>
   </text>
